==Russian==

===Etymology===
From {{der|ru|grc|τόρμος||socket into which a pin or peg is inserted}}, from {{der|ru|ine-pro|*tórmos||hole}}, from {{der|ru|ine-pro|*terh₁-|*ter-|to rub, bore, twist}} (whence also {{cog|ru|тере́ть}}
[https://books.google.ca/books?id=Ea8jAQAAIAAJ&dq=wade+word+origin+russian&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwinns7-yITcAhWBWLwKHXwNA9EQ6AEILjAB See ''Russian etymological dictionary''—Terence R. Wade, Terence Leslie Brian Wade].

Oleg Trubachev thinks Greek origin is unlikely. Nikolai Dmitriev suggests adoption from [[Turkic]] [[turmaz]] ("not stoppable" or "pad for the wheel of waggon"). [https://books.google.az/books/about/%D0%9B%D0%B5%D0%BA%D1%81%D0%B8%D0%BA%D0%BE%D0%B3%D1%80%D0%B0%D1%84%D0%B8%D1%87%D0%B5%D1%81%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%B9_%D1%81.html?id=G644bwAACAAJ&redir_esc=y See «Лексикографический сборник», 3, 1958, p. 45]

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|то́рмоз}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-тормоз.ogg}}

